<td id="S4.T2.4.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;"><span id="S4.T2.4.1.5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2FFF2;">106</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T2.4.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T2.4.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:8.0pt;padding-right:8.0pt;" colspan="5"><span id="S4.T2.4.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Eligibility Check: 100% of queries satisfy <math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}|\geq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∩</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}|\geq 5</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">No candidate truncation is applied: all methods rank the full intersection pool <math id="S4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∩</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}</annotation></semantics></math> per query. This avoids introducing method-specific biases arising from heuristic pre-filtering.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3. </span>Ranking performance on NGR-33k (<math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>). We compare <span id="S4.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unsupervised Baselines</span>, <span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Teacher–Student Distillation</span>, and <span id="S4.T3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Judge-B supervised</span> methods. <span id="S4.T3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> indicates the best performing model. Note that the Distilled Student outperforms the Teacher (Cross-Encoder).</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.10" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:172pt;vertical-align:-83.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-21.7pt,10.8pt) scale(0.888210234331588,0.888210234331588) ;">
