<div id="S4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Story Generation and Query Grouping:</em> Stories are generated offline under structured constraints <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> using a fixed prompt template. Each story is stored with a unique <span id="S4.SS1.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">story_id</span> (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.1. Data and Query Construction ‣ 4. Experiments and Results ‣ Mitigating Preference Leakage via Strict Estimator Separation for Normative Generative Ranking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and we deterministically derive a <span id="S4.SS1.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">query_id</span> from the constraint triple to group stories into within-query candidate pools <math id="S4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
