<td id="S4.T6.4.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.75pt 8.0pt;"><math id="S4.T6.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.582" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.582</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.582</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.T6.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm.04</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T6.4.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.75pt 8.0pt;"><math id="S4.T6.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.552" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.552</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.552</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.T6.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm.06</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T6.4.1.10.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.75pt 8.0pt;"><math id="S4.T6.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.570" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.570</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.570</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.T6.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.700em">.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm.04</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Comparative Models</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate three classes of ranking strategies. All methods rank candidates within the strictly defined intersection pool <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>∩</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{q}^{\cap}</annotation></semantics></math> and are evaluated exclusively against Judge A labels (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">1. Unsupervised Baselines:</em> To measure the difficulty of the task without normative supervision, we employ:
<span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random:</span> A uniform random permutation (lower bound). <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lexical Rankers:</span> We evaluate <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BM25</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Robertson and Zaragoza, 2009</a>)</cite>, <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPH</span> (Divergence-from-Randomness) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Amati and van Rijsbergen, 2002</a>)</cite>, and <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dirichlet LM</span> (<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu{=}2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu{=}2000</annotation></semantics></math>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhai and Lafferty, 2004</a>)</cite>. All lexical models score a pseudo-query derived from the constraint string <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{age},\text{moral},\text{culture})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>age</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>moral</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>culture</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{age},\text{moral},\text{culture})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7. </span>Pairwise ranker performance vs. training data fraction. <span id="S4.T7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F2FFF2;">Full Supervision</span> is required for significant gains.</figcaption>
